# Security (fit)

- Validate request data at API boundaries using Zod before business logic executes.
- API responses must follow the standard envelope — see `api-contracts.mdc`.
- Return generic error messages to clients; keep detailed diagnostics internal.
- Fail closed on auth/authz uncertainty; verify ownership before mutations.

## Don't

- Trust client-side checks as a substitute for server-side authorization.
- Expose stack traces or database details in API responses.
- Log tokens, passwords, or personal data.
